  {
   "@id": "urn:soundlore:facet:PRD",
   "@type": "skos:Collection",
   "prefLabel": "Production and sound",
   "notation": "PRD",
   "definition": "This facet covers recording choices, audio processing, sampling, sound design, and production aesthetics that shape the audible character of music.",
   "scopeNote": "Production shapes how performed or constructed sounds become a recording or amplified presentation. Decisions about capture, editing, processing, balance, and space can change the listener’s experience substantially. Production may preserve the impression of an immediate performance or create a sound that could not arise from an unprocessed ensemble. Its contribution is audible even when listeners cannot identify the equipment or methods involved.\n\nThe facet organizes these choices through several branches. Recording aesthetic and Era aesthetic describe broad sonic approaches and historical references. Dynamics processing concerns signal-level control, while Spatial effects creates or modifies perceived space. Modulation effects, Distortion, Filters, and Pitch effects alter different properties of sound. Time manipulation changes timing, duration, or playback direction. Sampling reuses recorded material, and Sound design develops sounds for particular musical roles.\n\nProduction practices can help distinguish styles. Dub frequently gives echo and reverberation an active musical role. Some punk recordings emphasize a direct, relatively rough presentation. Contemporary pop often uses detailed editing and layered vocal production. These are tendencies, and recordings within each tradition can differ widely.\n\nThis facet concerns how sound is captured, transformed, and presented. The performer’s physical actions belong in Instrumental techniques or Voice and vocal technique. Musical loudness and articulation as expressive performance choices belong in Dynamics and articulation. Historical sound labels describe selected production traits rather than everything recorded during a particular decade.",
   "member": [
